---
title: Magic Faux-Tisserie Chicken
servings: 4
Rating: 9/10
description: "This chicken is the most perfect, insanely tender, unapologetically moist chicken you will ever make. Slow-roasting the bird at a low temperature yields the same fall-off-the-bone meat as a rotisserie, and the spice-rubbed skin is a dreamy combination of crisp and sticky."
source: The Dude Diet
tags: Chicken
---

Preheat the oven to 300°F.
Remove any giblets and pieces from the cavity of the @whole chicken{3.5%lb},
then rinse the chicken thoroughly with cold water, and dry it well with paper towels.

In a small bowl, combine the @smoked paprika{2.5%tsp}, @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @light brown sugar{2%tsp},
@chili powder{1.5%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, @garlic powder{1/2%tsp}, and @ground cumin{1/4%tsp}. 

Carefully run your fingers under the skin on the breasts of your bird.
Rub the breasts underneath the skin with @olive oil{1%tbsp} and 1 teaspoon of the spice mixture.
Rub the remaining @olive oil{2%tbsp} on the chicken's skin, and season the bird all over with the remaining spice mixture.

Stuff the cavity with the @garlic{5%cloves}(smashed) and @lemon{1/2}(quartered) quarters.
Tie the legs together with #kitchen twine{} and place the bird breast side up in a #roasting pan{}.

Roast the chicken about ~{3%hours} (depending on the size of the bird),
basting at the 1h30m and 2h30m marks (no need for a baster, just spoon the juices over the bird)
or until the meat is very tender and the skin is dark brown. 

Let the chicken rest for 10 minutes before carving and serving.
